    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0456" n="372" xml:id="pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 614.119/111</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leavell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-16T12:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 16, 1918, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received October 17, 11.22 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My cipher telegram September 20, 10 a.m. Governmental decree has just been issued
                    empowering Custodian Hodgsdon to sell the German-owned
                    Empresa Electrica de Guatemala.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d416-f1"/> Text of decree
                    follows by next mail.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leavell</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d416-f1" n="1" xml:id="d416-f1-content">
                <p>Note in file: “Telephoned to A. J. R. Mitchell to release
                    goods to Electrica de Guatemala. J.G.L.” (Julius
                        G. Lay, Acting Foreign Trade Adviser of the Department of
                    State.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
